## Gate and importer evidence

- The final inventory/canonicaljson/provhost harness applied and ran 29 narrowings individually. All 29 were killed by their named test; one harmless comment control survived. This includes a token-preserving identity-validation mutant: the static source census passed while the behavioral suite failed at `TestClassifyRefusesIdentityDigestMismatch`.
- The separate `internal/rpcwire` harness killed all seven delegated inventory-validator narrowings; its neutral control passed.
- The importer grid records base and candidate direct importer sets, per-entry input classes and outcomes, and every moved class in `internal/merkleinventory/IMPORTER-OUTCOMES.md`. The changed `canonicaljson` importer set grows from 22 to 23 and `rpcwire` from 3 to 4 through the new package. The exact production identity owner path was added to the `provhost` source-test allowlist; no production `provhost` importer was added.
- The Story-owned shared registry `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json` is unchanged.

See `TASK-260830-nxqqaw_conformance-matrix.md` for the gate × production entry × axis table, class tables, named tests, narrowings, and stated bounds.

## Validation run

All 45 candidate Go package paths were covered by six bounded test groups. The full verbose suite, coverage suite, and race suite exited 0. After the last code/test change, `canonicaljson` and `merkleinventory` race runs were repeated individually and the final group 6 race run was repeated. Coverage reports `internal/canonicaljson` at 96.8% and `internal/merkleinventory` at 80.3%.

