The first directives read used the stale worktree board config and failed, so directives were unknown at that point. Two subsequent reads against the authoritative `$TASK_BOARD_DIR` succeeded and reported no directives; raw CLI logs are included in the evidence archive. The task object remains in `development` until the requested developer handoff.

## Handoff state

All tracked changes are in the managed Story worktree and remain uncommitted and unstaged for the Change Request snapshot. No task-board file was edited directly. The task-scoped result, matrix, and compact evidence archive are attached as outcome resources before invoking the developer handoff.

The required `task-board handoff TASK-260830-nxqqaw --role developer` command was invoked. It exited 1 with `cannot hand off TASK-260830-nxqqaw: unchecked checklist items [1 7] ...: handoff evidence missing`. The task remains blocked pending resolution of the exact gaps recorded in `TASK-260830-nxqqaw_blocker.md`; it has not moved to `to-review`.

After recording the blocker, `set_status(..., status=blocked)` moved TASK-260830-nxqqaw from `development` to `blocked`. The task-board CLI also automatically demoted parent STORY-260830-ub60id and EPIC-260830-3v9jlg from `development` to `to-dev`; no direct parent status mutation was made. The refreshed evidence archive is 616,022 bytes and remains under the 1 MiB limit. Four outcome resources (results, conformance matrix, evidence archive, blocker) were read back byte-identically.

